{"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree decomposition by the minimum fill-in heuristic: repeatedly eliminate the vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose neighbors lack the fewest edges to form a clique, making them one; stop when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"remaining vertices form a clique. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"width"},{"type":"text","text":" is an upper bound on the treewidth, and is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the treewidth of a chordal graph."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"treewidthMinFillIn()","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P7CliquesE18treewidthMinFillInAD17TreeDecompositionVy6VertexQzGyF","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"treewidthMinFillIn"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TreeDecomposition","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Cliques17TreeDecompositionV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/TreeDecomposition.swift#L162","fileName":"TreeDecomposition.swift"},"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Cliques"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/treewidthMinFillIn()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"treewidthMinFillIn"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifi